## What it is

A team strategy game with a large roster of heroes and many ways to build a match-winning plan.

## Before you install

Checked 23 November 2026. Steam lists Valve as developer and publisher, with a release date of 9 July 2013. The base game is free to play, with in-app purchases. The minimum column asks for Windows 7 or newer, a dual-core Intel or AMD processor at 2.8 GHz, 4 GB of memory, an NVIDIA GeForce 8600/9600GT or ATI/AMD Radeon HD2600/3600, DirectX 11, a broadband connection, and 60 GB of storage. Valve Anti-Cheat is enabled. Steam’s content notice mentions fantasy violence, use of alcohol, and mild partial nudity.

Dota 2 is a team hero-strategy game, not a battle royale. Steam’s app details, checked 8 November 2026, list Windows, macOS, and Linux for the free base game. Confirm that list and the system requirements on the Steam page before you install.

## Official installation and support

Follow the official store link above for installation and updates. GameNews does not host game files. If installation fails, record the error and your hardware details before consulting the publisher's support resources.

